    <string name="help_title">Help</string>
    <string name="help_intro">Field abbreviations and calculated values used in the log.</string>
    <string name="help_section_general">General</string>
    <string name="help_general_content">• Cdr — aircraft commander.\n• 2nd pilot (navigator) — second pilot or navigator.\n• Unit — unit or squadron.\n• Aircraft type / no. — aircraft type and registration.\n• Log no. — navigation log number.\n• Date — flight date.</string>
    <string name="help_section_wind">Wind</string>
    <string name="help_wind_content">• Point — point for which the wind is given.\n• H — altitude for which the wind is given.\n• δ — true wind direction (from which the wind blows).\n• U — wind speed.\n• ΔM — magnetic declination.\n• δn — navigational (magnetic) wind direction (towards which the wind blows): δn = δ − ΔM ± 180°.</string>
    <string name="help_section_weather">Weather</string>
    <string name="help_weather_content">• Weather valid for — validity period (hours and minutes).\n• Landing MH — magnetic landing heading.\n• Friction — runway friction coefficient.\n• δ — surface wind direction (from which the wind blows).\n• U — surface wind speed.\n• DA — decision altitude.\n• Visibility — visibility.\n• P — atmospheric pressure.\n• Obstacle alt. — obstacle height in the weather block.\n• t — air temperature.\n• δ and U in the weather block are surface wind; route calculations use the wind from the Wind group.</string>
    <string name="help_section_logbook">Flight log</string>
    <string name="help_logbook_content">• P min. reduced — minimum reduced pressure used for flight level selection.\n• Assigned level — assigned flight level or altitude.</string>
    <string name="help_section_aerodromes">Aerodromes</string>
    <string name="help_aerodromes_content">• δ — aerodrome magnetic declination.\n• U — aerodrome wind speed.\n• P0 — aerodrome pressure.\n• t0 — aerodrome temperature.\n• MAC — mean aerodynamic chord.\n• Takeoff / landing mass.\n• Vr — rotation speed.\n• Vapp — indicated approach speed.\n• Vtd — touchdown speed.\n• Takeoff / landing run.\n• Safe circle alt. — safe circle altitude.</string>
    <string name="help_section_route">Route</string>
    <string name="help_route_content">• Terrain alt. — terrain elevation.\n• Obstacle alt. — obstacle height.\n• Safe alt. corr. — corrected safe altitude.\n• Route — waypoint name.\n• MT — magnetic track.\n• MH — magnetic heading.\n• TAS — true airspeed.\n• GS — ground speed.\n• Dist — leg distance (manual).\n• t — calculated leg time.\n• Q calc — calculated fuel remaining.\n• Q actual — actual fuel remaining or consumption (manual).\n• T calc / T actual — calculated and actual time (manual).\n• Alt. — flight level or altitude (manual).\n• Notes — free note.</string>
    <string name="help_section_fuel">Fuel</string>
    <string name="help_fuel_content">• Q ground — fuel for taxi and ground operations.\n• Q unusable — unusable fuel.\n• Q60 — 60-minute fuel reserve.\n• q/h — hourly fuel consumption.\n• t ldg — time allowed for landing.\n• ρ(Q) — fuel density.</string>
    <string name="help_section_actual">Flight execution</string>
    <string name="help_actual_content">• Actual flight time — actual time; of which night — night time.\n• Go-around from DA to alternate — S and Q for go-around from decision altitude.\n• Diversion point to alternate — S div. and Q div. for return to alternate.</string>
    <string name="help_section_sun">Sun</string>
    <string name="help_sun_content">• Sunrise and sunset — times for the specified point.\n• Sum — value from tables or calculation for the point; entered manually.</string>
    <string name="help_section_calculations">Calculations</string>
    <string name="help_calculations_content">• δn = δ − ΔM ± 180°.\n• Wind angle = δn − MT.\n• Drift = asin(U · sin(wind angle) / TAS).\n• MH = MT − drift.\n• GS — ground speed from the wind triangle.\n• t = Dist / GS × 60, rounded up to the minute.\n• Q calc — from the Q60 reserve upwards along the route using q/h and leg times.\n• Safe alt. corr. = 100 + obstacle − ((t0 − 15) / 300) · (100 + obstacle).</string>
    <string name="help_disclaimer">This help is for reference only and does not replace official documents, aircraft manuals or applicable regulations. Verify all calculations before flight.</string>
</resources>

